4.9 Master/detail
A list and a form that edits the selected entry is called master/detail. It needs one more view model property for the selected item, bound to the list’s SelectedItem:
[ObservableProperty]
private Person? _selectedPerson;
&lt;ListBox ItemsSource="{Binding People}" SelectedItem="{Binding SelectedPerson}"/&gt;
The form binds through that property with a path: {Binding SelectedPerson.FirstName}. Because Person announces its changes, editing the name in the form updates the list entry at the same time.
As long as nothing is selected, the form should be hidden. A converter turns the selected person into a bool; Avalonia has a ready-made one for this check:
&lt;StackPanel IsVisible="{Binding SelectedPerson, Converter={x:Static ObjectConverters.IsNotNull}}"&gt;






TipLab 4.8: Master/detail



🎯 Goal. Selecting a person opens a form to edit the name.

Add the SelectedPerson property from above to the view model, and bind the list’s SelectedItem to it.
Below the ListBox, add the detail form:
&lt;StackPanel Grid.Row="1" Margin="0,16,0,0" Spacing="4"
            IsVisible="{Binding SelectedPerson, Converter={x:Static ObjectConverters.IsNotNull}}"&gt;
